        {
            "type": "patchouli:crafting",
            "recipe": "firmalife:crafting/oven_insulation",
            "text": "Crafting oven insulation for your Bottom Oven allows you to remove the need for insulating it on the sides and back. It does not remove the need for the chimney or to insulate top ovens. Use $(item)$(k:key.use)$() to apply it."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
            "title": "Aesthetics",
            "anchor": "countertop",
            "item": "firmalife:brick_countertop,firmalife:rustic_countertop,firmalife:tile_countertop,firmalife:stone_countertop,firmalife:rustic_finish,firmalife:tile_finish,firmalife:stone_finish",
            "text": "$(thing)Countertops$() and $(thing)Finishes$() are aesthetic blocks that count as oven parts. Finishes are applied with $(item)$(k:key.use)$(). Only $(n)brick$() oven blocks may take on finishes. Stone finish can't be applied to brick. Use $(item)Sealed bricks$() to match the look."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
            "title": "Oven Hopper",
            "anchor": "oven_hopper",
            "item": "firmalife:oven_hopper",
            "text": "The $(thing)Oven Hopper$() will input logs into any Bottom Oven that it is facing. It holds 16 logs (4 stacks of 4, like a log pile), and its inventory is fed by dropping items in the top. Item pipes are capable of doing the same thing, but they cannot act as insulation."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
            "title": "Ashtray",
            "anchor": "ashtray",
            "item": "firmalife:ashtray",
            "text": "The $(thing)Ashtray$() collects $(thing)Wood Ash$() when placed below a $(thing)Bottom Oven Block$(). There is a 0.5 chance it gains ash when fuel is consumed. Ash is extracted with $(item)$(k:key.use)$() or hoppers, and inserted via $(item)$(k:key.attack)$() it."
        },
