        {
            "title": "Appliances",
            "anchor": "appliances",
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "text": "$(thing)Appliances$() are devices that can be $(l:game_mechanics/heating#temps)Heated$() to run recipes. All appliances use the same system for heating which means you can mix and match which $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#heat_sources)Heat Source$() you want to use.$(li)$(bold)$(l:cooking/cooking_methods#fire_box_top_oven)Fire Box Top Oven$()$(li)$(bold)$(l:cooking/cooking_methods#copper_pot)Copper Pot$()$(li2)$(l:cooking/cooking_methods#condenser)Condenser$()$(li)$(bold)$(l:cooking/cooking_methods#skillet)Skillet$()$(bold)$(li)$(l:cooking/cooking_methods#baking_dish)Baking Dish$()"
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
            "anchor": "fire_box_top_oven",
            "item": "tfg:fire_box_top_oven",
            "title": "Fire Box Top Oven",
            "link_recipes": false,
            "text": "Despite its name, a $(thing)Fire Box Top Oven$() can be heated by more than just the $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#fire_box)Fire Box$().$(br)Consider this device as a mix between a $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#top_oven)Top Oven$() and a $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#grill)Grill$() while providing a better $(l:cooking/decay#table)Decay Modifier$() than either. Fire box top ovens have 9 slots instead of 4 and do not require insulation or chimneys."
        },
