        {
            "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
            "anchor": "condenser",
            "item": "tfg:condenser",
            "title": "Condenser",
            "link_recipes": false,
            "text": "The $(thing)Condenser$() is an attachment for the $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#copper_pot)Copper Pot$() used for distilling liquids. When placed above the copper pot, running any condensing recipes will result in their vapors condensing in the top block and flowing out of the spigot face. Fluid containers, such as a $(l:craftsmanship/barrels)Barrel$() can be placed against the spigot or right below it to collect the fluid. Otherwise, it will be void."
        },
        {
            "type": "tfg:multimultiblock",
            "name": "",
            "text": "Some recipes will require coolants to be added to the condenser. Which can be specific fluids, or depend on their inherent temperature (K).",
